The Windows owner process tracker adapts the narrow missing-process error
classification from psutil at a1e3067965a075c40b79971cfda51501e80da685.
The implementation is independent; the unmodified proc_utils.c reference and
BSD-3-Clause license are preserved under third_party/reference-sources/psutil.
Original copyright: Jay Loden, Dave Daeschler, Giampaolo Rodola and contributors.
Access-denied errors are not treated as process-exit evidence.

TaskStore verification follows SQLite's documented locking, read-only recovery
and WAL contracts. A conservative super-journal suffix refusal uses the existing
format described in SQLite 3.45.1 pager.c at
189e44dfecdc7868bb860dfb5d98eab371318c37. That public-domain source and its original
LICENSE.md are preserved in third_party/reference-sources/sqlite/. SQLite itself
performs recovery; no copied pager implementation is part of the Python runtime.
